<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burgdorf</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burgdorf is a town in the Swiss canton of Bern, on the Emme at the entrance to the Emmental. It grew below a castle of the dukes of Zähringen, passed to the counts of Kyburg in 1218 and was bought by Bern in 1384. The educator <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/johann-heinrich-pestalozzi">Johann Heinrich Pestalozzi</a> ran his pioneering school in Burgdorf Castle from 1800 to 1804.</p></div>
